.TH env_get2 3
.SH NAME
env_get2 \- retrieve an environment variable value from a custom array
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B const char* env_get2(const char* const* \fIenvp\fP, const char* \fIs\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_get2
searches the null-terminated environment array \fIenvp\fP for an 
environment variable named \fIs\fP. It looks for a string in 
\fIenvp\fP that starts with \fIs\fP followed immediately by an '=' 
character.

.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer to the value part of the environment variable (the string 
following the '='), or NULL if the variable was not found.